==English==

===Etymology===
{{etymon|en|:inh|enm:*manage<ety:bor<fro:manege<ety:der<roa-oit:maneggiare<unc>>>>>|tree=1}}
From {{inh|en|en-ear|manage|nocat=1}}, {{m|en|menage}}, from {{inh|en|enm|*manage}}, {{m|enm|*menage}}, from {{der|en|fro|manege||the handling or training of a horse, horsemanship, riding, maneuvers, proceedings}}, probably from {{der|en|roa-oit|maneggiare||to handle, manage, touch, treat}}, from {{der|en|la-vul|*manizāre|t=handle}}, from {{der|en|la|manus|t=hand}} + {{m|la|-izō|-izāre|pos=verb-forming suffix}}. {{doublet|en|manège}}.

Compare typologically {{m+|en|handle}}; {{m+|ru|руководи́ть}} (< {{m|ru|рука́}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈmæn.ɪd͡ʒ/|a=RP}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-manage.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{a|en|US}}
** {{IPA|en|/ˈmæn.ɪd͡ʒ/|a=GenAm,CA,non-weak vowel}}
** {{IPA|en|/ˈmɛən.ɪd͡ʒ/|a=æ-raising}}
*** {{audio|en|en-us-manage.ogg}}
** {{IPA|en|/ˈmæn.əd͡ʒ/|a=weak vowel}}
** {{IPA|en|/ˈmɛən.əd͡ʒ/|a=æ-raising}}
